</figure>
<div id="S2.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Advantages of Multi-Physics benchmark.</span> Compared to existing physics reasoning benchmarks, Multi-Physics offers a more comprehensive and diverse evaluation framework. While prior datasets like PHYBench <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>]</cite> and ABench-Physics <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">33</a>]</cite> lack visual inputs, and others such as PHYSICS <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">38</a>]</cite> or PhysReason <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>]</cite> are limited in subject coverage, Multi-Physics bridges these gaps by combining 1,412 questions with 1,438 images across 11 subjects. This balance of multimodal data and wide-ranging physics subjects enables more robust evaluation of models’ conceptual understanding and physics problem-solving abilities, as shown in Table <a href="#S2.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 2.1 Multi-Physics Construction ‣ 2 Methods ‣ Multi-Physics: A Comprehensive Benchmark for Multimodal LLMs Reasoning on Chinese Multi-subject Physics Problems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
